{"source":"\u0022\u0022\u0022Hashes and generators written the idiomatic Python way: an int masked to emulate a register. Written for this repository (O0062).\u0022\u0022\u0022\n\n\ndef fnv1a64(value: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022FNV-1a, 64 bits, over the 8 bytes of a value, the lowest first.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    rest = value \u0026 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n    h = 0xCBF29CE484222325\n    for _ in range(8):\n        h ^= rest \u0026 0xFF\n        h = (h * 0x100000001B3) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n        rest \u003E\u003E= 8\n    return h\n\n\ndef fnv1a32(value: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022FNV-1a, 32 bits, over the 4 bytes of a value, the lowest first.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    rest = value \u0026 0xFFFFFFFF\n    h = 0x811C9DC5\n    for _ in range(4):\n        h ^= rest \u0026 0xFF\n        h = (h * 16777619) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFF\n        rest \u003E\u003E= 8\n    return h\n\n\ndef splitmix64(seed: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022One output of SplitMix64 for a state.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    z = (seed \u002B 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n    z = ((z ^ (z \u003E\u003E 30)) * 0xBF58476D1CE4E5B9) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n    z = ((z ^ (z \u003E\u003E 27)) * 0x94D049BB133111EB) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n    return z ^ (z \u003E\u003E 31)\n\n\ndef xorshift64(state: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022One step of Marsaglia\u0027s xorshift64 (13, 7, 17).\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    x = state \u0026 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n    x ^= (x \u003C\u003C 13) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n    x ^= x \u003E\u003E 7\n    x ^= (x \u003C\u003C 17) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n    return x\n\n\ndef xorshift32_sum(seed: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022Sixteen steps of xorshift32 (13, 17, 5), their outputs summed modulo 2**32.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    x = (seed \u0026 0xFFFFFFFF) | 1\n    total = 0\n    for _ in range(16):\n        x ^= (x \u003C\u003C 13) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFF\n        x ^= x \u003E\u003E 17\n        x ^= (x \u003C\u003C 5) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFF\n        total = (total \u002B x) % 4294967296\n    return total\n\n\ndef checksum() -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022A checksum of the numbers below 1000, which needs no parameter.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(1000):\n        total = (total * 31 \u002B i) \u0026 0xFFFF\n    return total\n\n\ndef unmasked_product(a: int, b: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022A product used unmasked as well as masked: it stays exact.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    product = a * b\n    low = product \u0026 0xFFFFFFFF\n    return low \u002B product\n\n\ndef quotient_low(a: int, b: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022A floor division inside a mask: the low bits of a quotient depend on the high bits of the dividend.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    return (a // b) \u0026 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n\ndef shifted_low(a: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u0022A right shift inside a mask pulls in bits above the mask.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    return (a \u003E\u003E 3) \u0026 0xFF\n\n\ndef power(n: int) -\u003E int:\n    \u0022\u0022\u00222 ** n, which exceeds 64 bits from n = 64 on.\u0022\u0022\u0022\n    return 2 ** n\n","dump":{"format":1,"module":{"_":"Module","body":[{"_":"Expr","line":1,"col":1,"endLine":1,"endCol":136,"value":{"_":"Constant","line":1,"col":1,"endLine":1,"endCol":136,"kind":"str","value":"Hashes and generators written the idiomatic Python way: an int masked to emulate a register. Written for this repository (O0062)."}},{"_":"FunctionDef","line":4,"col":1,"endLine":12,"endCol":13,"name":"fnv1a64","args":{"_":"arguments","posonlyargs":[],"args":[{"_":"arg","line":4,"col":13,"endLine":4,"endCol":23,"arg":"value","annotation":{"_":"Name","line":4,"col":20,"endLine":4,"endCol":23,"id":"int","ctx":{"_":"Load"}}}],"vararg":null,"kwonlyargs":[],"kw_defaults":[],"kwarg":null,"defaults":[]},"body":[{"_":"Expr","line":5,"col":5,"endLine":5,"endCol":74,"value":{"_":"Constant","line":5,"col":5,"endLine":5,"endCol":74,"kind":"str","value":"FNV-1a, 64 bits, over the 8 by